---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"mcp\", \"--help\"])"
---
Serve the tools of Sluice to an MCP client over standard input and output

The tools send, receive, inspect, list jobs, report a job, cancel and run the doctor. They work inside the folders named with `--root` and nowhere else, and with none they refuse every send and receive. A send returns a ticket, which is a secret and which the client's transcript then holds. The server ends when its input closes.

Usage: sluice mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --root <DIR>
          A folder the tools may send from and receive into, written as a tool names it; repeat for more. Without one every send and receive is refused

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

      --relay <URL>
          The relay that carries a transfer when a direct path fails

      --n0-relays
          Use n0's public relays and DNS discovery (not run by this project)

      --loopback
          Use 127.0.0.1 only, with no relay, no mDNS, no port mapping and no address publishing. It cannot be combined with `--relay` or `--n0-relays`

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
